+## Current Resumption and Parent Audit — 2026-10-28
+
+The advisory implementation and supplemental Tenants/Conversations fixes are already landed in the current clean owner checkouts; no source patch is needed in this resumption. Accepted CLI 4.38.1 now implements `prepare-build`: source preparation and the actual mapped Conversations.Server.Tests Debug build pass, with zero warnings/errors. The six focused owner classes pass 243 unique tests, zero failures/errors/skips/not-run. Parent independently inspected the raw XML/build summaries, verified all 47 recorded source hashes and the initial 14 evidence hashes, and ran 37 passing planning-guard tests plus both authority validators. Current evidence totals 280 passing tests; the original frozen block and canonical baseline remain unchanged. Exact commands, environment, raw receipts and current revisions: [resumption evidence](evidence/6-4-advisory-resolution-20261021/resumption-20261028/README.md).
+
+Package preparation exits 2 with HXW011 (the local Platform identity has no local SemVer release tag) and HXW009 (Platform pins Builds `51a71cb1cfe860d5fc135eb3b8521fd80c413810`, whereas the umbrella index/checkout selects `1745ea0f09df9e518aeea3eeb1a7df836f67e09d`). This run did not refresh remote CI or official publication; local tag absence is not proof of official release absence. The older 4.35.2 missing-command blocker is superseded by this current evidence.
+
+Current Projects.Server.Tests and the narrower Contracts.Tests source builds refuse missing producer-selected Conversations mapping. Reusing the actual Conversations mapping correctly refuses the Projects root with HXW006. The accepted command has no active-module/entry-project override and Projects has no existing module declaration. No consumer mapping, new enrollment or runtime migration was invented. Accordingly, current full Projects/gateway/store matrix acceptance is incomplete; historical receipts are not new current-tree acceptance. Step 3 cannot advance to final workflow review/completion while these requirements remain unmet.
+
+Story status stays `in-progress`. Qualified Platform/Builds package preparation, a supported Projects verification route, successful current-source CI, separately approved Conversations publication, official package verification and verified consumer pins remain delivery requirements. Only this specification checkpoint and evidence changed; no source, dependency/tool pin, Git index/ref, remote, runtime or deployment changed. The original frozen boundary and separate publication approval remain in force.
